    "result": "Dependency resolution passed. Every wiki-master skill the callers name resolved, the JSON block has no stale or missing names, and every caller reference I checked exists. I only read files and invoked skills. I ran no helpers, searched no vault and wrote nothing. The Glob tool was denied in this mode, so I used direct Read calls on known paths instead.\n\n## wiki-master skills the callers require\n\n| Skill | Callers that name it |\n|---|---|\n| `wiki-master:wiki-search` | spec-plan (grounding, step 3); plugin-map (\"Wiki retrieval\" row) |\n| `wiki-master:wiki-researcher` | spec-plan (gap discovery and ingestion of named clippings, step 3) |\n| `wiki-master:wiki-project` | spec-plan (saving the spec, step 9); q-master (record step 6); plugin-map (\"Document authoring and roadmap\" and \"Writing or validating project documents\" rows) |\n| `wiki-master:wiki-setup` | plugin-map (\"Wiki checks and scaffolding\", \"Writing or validating project documents\" and \"Reporting wiki health\" rows) |\n| `wiki-master:wiki-maintainer` | No caller names it by qualified skill. It appears only in the JSON block and as one of the six roles in the plugin-map dependency prose. |\n| `wiki-master:wiki-purge` | No caller names it by qualified skill. Same as `wiki-maintainer`. |\n\nI invoked the four skills the callers name explicitly. I did not invoke `wiki-maintainer` or `wiki-purge`, since no caller calls them directly.\n\n## Resolution results\n\nAll four resolved with no errors. Each loaded from `<CANDIDATE>\\skills\\<skill>`:\n- `wiki-master:wiki-search`: \"Launching skill: wiki-master:wiki-search\"\n- `wiki-master:wiki-researcher`: \"Launching skill: wiki-master:wiki-researcher\"\n- `wiki-master:wiki-project`: \"Launching skill: wiki-master:wiki-project\"\n- `wiki-master:wiki-setup`: \"Launching skill: wiki-master:wiki-setup\"\n\n## JSON block (agent-unreal `sibling-skills.json`)\n\nThe block lists `wiki-maintainer`, `wiki-project`, `wiki-purge`, `wiki-researcher`, `wiki-search` and `wiki-setup`. I compared these to the session catalog:\n- **Match:** all six names are in the catalog, which also lists exactly those six.\n- **Stale:** none.\n- **Missing:** none.\n- **Candidate file check:** `skills/wiki-maintainer/SKILL.md` exists with `name: wiki-maintainer`. I did not invoke it.\n\n## Direct reference checks\n\n- **spec-plan:** `references/spec-template.md` and `references/evidence.md` both exist.\n- **q-master:** `references/note-template.md` exists.\n- **plugin-map:** the \"Project state brief\" row names wiki-master's `scripts/session-brief.mjs`. It exists in the candidate plugin at `scripts/session-brief.mjs`. I did not check the 0.73.0 version minimum.\n\n## What each changed caller sends to the role\n\n- **spec-plan to `wiki-search`:** a read-only search of the project's wiki for relevant knowledge and roadmap items. It must report coverage and gaps, and the skill must not write anything.\n- **spec-plan to `wiki-researcher`:** when coverage is light, topic discovery for the gaps, then ingestion of the resulting named clippings. It runs under the user's existing authorization, and the skill proposes it first.\n- **spec-plan to `wiki-project`:** save the finished spec as `wiki/authored/<project>/backlog/<slug>.md` with `kind: backlog-item` and `backlog-status: planned`. This is original project documentation.\n- **q-master to `wiki-project`:** write or edit `wiki/authored/<project>/notes/project-tooling.md` (`kind: note`) from the note template. If the project has no overview, create that first. It happens only after the user approves.\n- **game-studio plugin-map:**\n  - `wiki-search` handles read-only page lookup and cited answers.\n  - `wiki-project` handles original documents, the generated roadmap and required validation of changed pages.\n  - `wiki-setup` handles validation-only requests, whole-vault reports, diagnostics and initialization, with findings and coverage limits and no edits.\n- **agent-unreal `sibling-skills.json`:** it sends no task. It only declares the six-name wiki-master skill set.",
